cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "Tortoise: a p-type-only organic thin-film transistor time-race classifier (simulation study)"
version: v1.0
date-released: "2026-11-05"
authors:
  - family-names: Lopez
    given-names: Mikel
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-6281-6566"
repository-code: "https://example.org/REPLACE-WITH-REPOSITORY-URL"
abstract: >-
  Tortoise is a 6-input, 5-class linear classifier designed to be built only from p-type
  organic thin-film transistors (DNTT-family OTFTs on an AlOx/SAM dielectric, 134 transistors,
  single 3.3 V rail). Each class integrates its weighted input current onto a rail capacitor;
  then all rails race to a common threshold and the first to arrive latches and locks out the
  others. The repository holds the design (netlists, compact-model cards, specification), the
  simulation tooling, and the protocols, per-run data and reports of the ngspice simulation
  campaigns. Simulation only: nothing has been fabricated or measured, and the dataset is
  synthetic.
keywords:
  - organic electronics
  - OTFT
  - flexible electronics
  - time-domain computing
  - neuromorphic
  - ngspice
